1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:06,330
The SAT math section is built from
a list of exactly nineteen skills.

2
00:00:06,360 --> 00:00:08,339
The College Board publishes the list,

3
00:00:08,359 --> 00:00:10,490
split into four domains.

4
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:13,619
This video covers all nineteen, in order,

5
00:00:13,639 --> 00:00:17,290
with one SAT-style question for each.

6
00:00:17,743 --> 00:00:20,883
Pause on every question and
keep track of the ones you miss.

7
00:00:20,903 --> 00:00:25,753
Each miss points to one skill, and
that list becomes your study plan.

8
00:00:26,293 --> 00:00:27,953
One thing to notice first.

9
00:00:27,973 --> 00:00:31,793
Algebra and advanced math
have only eight of the skills,

10
00:00:31,813 --> 00:00:35,622
but together they're about
seventy percent of the questions.

11
00:00:36,143 --> 00:00:38,313
Domain one: algebra.

12
00:00:38,743 --> 00:00:41,243
About thirty-five percent of the section,

13
00:00:41,263 --> 00:00:45,313
and all five skills are
about linear relationships.

14
00:00:45,734 --> 00:00:48,633
Skill one: linear
equations in one variable.

15
00:00:48,653 --> 00:00:51,474
You'll solve them, build
them from word problems,

16
00:00:51,494 --> 00:00:53,953
and decide whether they have one solution,

17
00:00:53,973 --> 00:00:56,504
no solution, or infinitely many.

18
00:00:56,977 --> 00:01:00,796
In the equation two times the
quantity three x minus five,

19
00:01:00,816 --> 00:01:05,907
plus k, equals six x plus
four, k is a constant.

20
00:01:06,017 --> 00:01:09,317
If the equation has
infinitely many solutions,

21
00:01:09,337 --> 00:01:11,187
what is the value of k?

22
00:01:11,686 --> 00:01:13,176
Pause and try it.

23
00:01:18,947 --> 00:01:24,127
Distribute: six x minus ten
plus k equals six x plus four.

24
00:01:24,147 --> 00:01:26,287
The x terms already match.

25
00:01:26,307 --> 00:01:30,527
For infinitely many solutions,
the constants have to match too.

26
00:01:30,547 --> 00:01:34,957
Negative ten plus k equals
four, so k is fourteen.

27
00:01:35,411 --> 00:01:39,351
Desmos shortcut: graph
each side as y equals,

28
00:01:39,371 --> 00:01:41,661
and add a slider for k.

29
00:01:41,851 --> 00:01:45,710
The slider only runs from
negative ten to ten at first,

30
00:01:45,730 --> 00:01:48,220
so change its upper limit to twenty.

31
00:01:48,331 --> 00:01:52,741
Then drag until the two lines
sit exactly on top of each other.

32
00:01:53,188 --> 00:01:57,007
Skill two: linear
equations in two variables.

33
00:01:57,027 --> 00:02:00,528
These are usually word problems
with two unknown amounts.

34
00:02:00,548 --> 00:02:04,048
You'll write the equation,
explain what a number in it means,

35
00:02:04,068 --> 00:02:06,558
or find one amount when
you know the other.

36
00:02:06,983 --> 00:02:12,203
A bakery sells muffins for three dollars
each and loaves of bread for five

37
00:02:12,223 --> 00:02:13,323
dollars each.

38
00:02:13,343 --> 00:02:18,163
On Saturday, it earned one hundred
twenty dollars from muffins and bread,

39
00:02:18,183 --> 00:02:20,643
and it sold twenty-five muffins.

40
00:02:20,663 --> 00:02:23,113
How many loaves of bread did it sell?

41
00:02:23,582 --> 00:02:25,072
Pause and try it.

42
00:02:29,843 --> 00:02:35,023
The equation is three m plus
five b equals one hundred twenty.

43
00:02:35,043 --> 00:02:41,293
Plug in twenty-five muffins: seventy-five
plus five b equals one hundred twenty.

44
00:02:41,322 --> 00:02:46,933
So five b is forty-five,
and b is nine loaves.

45
00:02:47,422 --> 00:02:49,602
And if the question asks
what the five means,

46
00:02:49,622 --> 00:02:51,391
it's the price per loaf.

47
00:02:51,502 --> 00:02:55,711
Coefficients in these equations
are almost always rates.

48
00:02:56,196 --> 00:02:58,805
Skill three: linear functions.

49
00:02:58,915 --> 00:03:02,016
You get a table, a graph, or a story,

50
00:03:02,036 --> 00:03:07,126
and you find or interpret
f of x equals m x plus b.

51
00:03:07,355 --> 00:03:12,206
The slope is the rate of change,
and b is the starting value.

52
00:03:12,664 --> 00:03:15,923
A plumber charges a fixed
fee plus an hourly rate.

53
00:03:15,943 --> 00:03:20,723
The total charge is one hundred seventy
dollars for a two-hour job and three

54
00:03:20,743 --> 00:03:23,524
hundred thirty-five dollars
for a five-hour job.

55
00:03:23,544 --> 00:03:26,004
Which function gives the total charge,

56
00:03:26,024 --> 00:03:29,314
C of h, for an h-hour job?

57
00:03:30,364 --> 00:03:31,854
Pause and try it.

58
00:03:37,625 --> 00:03:41,484
The charge goes up one hundred
sixty-five dollars over three more hours,

59
00:03:41,504 --> 00:03:45,075
so the rate is fifty-five dollars an hour.

60
00:03:45,425 --> 00:03:50,084
The fee is one seventy
minus two times fifty-five,

61
00:03:50,104 --> 00:03:51,244
which is sixty.

62
00:03:51,264 --> 00:03:53,034
The answer is C.

63
00:03:53,508 --> 00:03:57,048
Desmos shortcut: put the
two points in a table,

64
00:03:57,068 --> 00:04:01,797
then type y one, tilde, m x one plus b.

65
00:04:02,108 --> 00:04:06,518
Desmos gives m equals
fifty-five and b equals sixty.

66
00:04:07,011 --> 00:04:11,711
Skill four: systems of two linear
equations in two variables.

67
00:04:11,731 --> 00:04:14,990
You'll solve them, set
them up from word problems,

68
00:04:15,010 --> 00:04:18,031
and sometimes decide if
there's one solution,

69
00:04:18,051 --> 00:04:20,820
no solution, or infinitely many.

70
00:04:21,278 --> 00:04:24,338
A school sold one hundred
fifty tickets to a play.

71
00:04:24,358 --> 00:04:29,178
Student tickets cost six dollars,
and adult tickets cost ten dollars.

72
00:04:29,198 --> 00:04:33,218
Total ticket sales were one
thousand one hundred forty dollars.

73
00:04:33,238 --> 00:04:35,687
How many adult tickets were sold?

74
00:04:36,129 --> 00:04:37,619
Pause and try it.

75
00:04:43,389 --> 00:04:49,889
s plus a equals one fifty, and six
s plus ten a equals eleven forty.

76
00:04:49,909 --> 00:04:53,848
Substitute s equals one fifty minus a.

77
00:04:53,868 --> 00:04:58,688
That gives nine hundred plus
four a equals eleven forty.

78
00:04:58,708 --> 00:05:02,719
So four a is two forty, and a is sixty.

79
00:05:03,156 --> 00:05:07,646
Desmos shortcut: type both
equations with x and y,

80
00:05:07,716 --> 00:05:10,016
zoom out, and click the intersection:

81
00:05:10,036 --> 00:05:11,695
ninety, sixty.

82
00:05:11,715 --> 00:05:13,526
Then answer what was asked.

83
00:05:13,635 --> 00:05:16,126
Adults are sixty, not ninety.

84
00:05:16,570 --> 00:05:21,150
Skill five: linear inequalities
in one or two variables.

85
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:24,230
At most means less than or equal to.

86
00:05:24,250 --> 00:05:27,139
At least means greater than or equal to.

87
00:05:27,290 --> 00:05:31,740
You'll also pick points that
satisfy a system of inequalities.

88
00:05:32,221 --> 00:05:36,671
A delivery van can carry at most
one thousand two hundred pounds.

89
00:05:36,741 --> 00:05:39,041
The driver weighs one
hundred eighty pounds,

90
00:05:39,061 --> 00:05:41,751
and each box weighs forty pounds.

91
00:05:42,141 --> 00:05:46,831
What is the greatest number of boxes
the van can carry along with the driver?

92
00:05:47,292 --> 00:05:48,782
Pause and try it.

93
00:05:53,553 --> 00:05:56,772
One eighty plus forty b
is at most twelve hundred.

94
00:05:56,792 --> 00:05:59,773
So forty b is at most one thousand twenty,

95
00:05:59,793 --> 00:06:03,453
and b is at most twenty-five point five.

96
00:06:03,473 --> 00:06:06,692
You can't carry half a box, so round down:

97
00:06:06,712 --> 00:06:07,723
twenty-five.

98
00:06:07,872 --> 00:06:09,563
The answer is A.

99
00:06:10,032 --> 00:06:12,331
Twenty-six is the rounding trap.

100
00:06:12,351 --> 00:06:15,532
It puts the van at twelve
hundred twenty pounds.

101
00:06:15,552 --> 00:06:17,922
And thirty forgets the driver.

102
00:06:18,422 --> 00:06:21,071
Domain two: advanced math.

103
00:06:21,221 --> 00:06:24,202
Also about thirty-five
percent of the section,

104
00:06:24,222 --> 00:06:25,642
but only three skills.

105
00:06:25,662 --> 00:06:28,032
So each one shows up a lot.

106
00:06:28,514 --> 00:06:32,123
Skill six: equivalent expressions.

107
00:06:32,353 --> 00:06:35,974
Expanding, factoring, combining fractions,

108
00:06:35,994 --> 00:06:39,083
and rewriting exponents and radicals.

109
00:06:39,354 --> 00:06:44,044
The usual question is, which
expression is equivalent to this one?

110
00:06:44,465 --> 00:06:49,525
Which expression is equivalent to
the quantity three x minus two,

111
00:06:49,545 --> 00:06:53,725
squared, minus the quantity x plus four,

112
00:06:53,745 --> 00:06:56,954
times the quantity x minus four?

113
00:06:57,377 --> 00:06:58,867
Pause and try it.

114
00:07:04,637 --> 00:07:11,137
Three x minus two, squared, is nine
x squared minus twelve x plus four.

115
00:07:11,157 --> 00:07:14,137
The product is x squared minus sixteen.

116
00:07:14,157 --> 00:07:18,657
Subtract all of it, so minus
sixteen becomes plus sixteen.

117
00:07:18,677 --> 00:07:22,977
That's eight x squared
minus twelve x plus twenty.

118
00:07:22,997 --> 00:07:24,847
The answer is B.

119
00:07:25,328 --> 00:07:28,107
A forgets to distribute the minus sign.

120
00:07:28,127 --> 00:07:30,108
C drops the middle term.

121
00:07:30,128 --> 00:07:33,547
In Desmos, graph the
original and each choice.

122
00:07:33,567 --> 00:07:36,897
Only the equivalent one
lands exactly on top.

123
00:07:37,326 --> 00:07:43,386
Skill seven: nonlinear equations in one
variable and systems of equations in two

124
00:07:43,406 --> 00:07:44,026
variables.

125
00:07:44,046 --> 00:07:47,746
That means quadratics,
radicals, rational equations,

126
00:07:47,766 --> 00:07:52,895
and absolute values, plus systems
like a line crossing a parabola.

127
00:07:53,321 --> 00:07:57,661
The system is y equals x
squared minus two x minus three,

128
00:07:57,681 --> 00:08:00,171
and y equals x plus seven.

129
00:08:00,441 --> 00:08:03,581
If the point a, b is a
solution to the system,

130
00:08:03,601 --> 00:08:07,531
and a is greater than zero,
what is the value of b?

131
00:08:07,998 --> 00:08:09,488
Pause and try it.

132
00:08:15,258 --> 00:08:18,037
Set them equal and move everything over:

133
00:08:18,057 --> 00:08:22,558
x squared minus three x
minus ten equals zero.

134
00:08:22,578 --> 00:08:27,147
That factors to x minus
five, times x plus two.

135
00:08:27,257 --> 00:08:32,758
a is positive, so a is five,
and b is five plus seven,

136
00:08:32,778 --> 00:08:34,028
which is twelve.

137
00:08:34,577 --> 00:08:38,597
Desmos shortcut: graph both
and click the intersections,

138
00:08:38,617 --> 00:08:42,027
negative two, five, and five, twelve.

139
00:08:42,337 --> 00:08:44,837
The trap is answering five, which is a,

140
00:08:44,857 --> 00:08:45,986
not b.

141
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:51,690
Skill eight: nonlinear functions,
mostly quadratic and exponential.

142
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:55,460
In a times b to the x,
a is the starting value,

143
00:08:55,480 --> 00:08:58,530
and b is what you multiply by each step.

144
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:02,569
For the function f, f of zero is six,

145
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:06,930
f of one is eighteen,
f of two is fifty-four,

146
00:09:07,079 --> 00:09:10,330
and f of three is one hundred sixty-two.

147
00:09:10,760 --> 00:09:13,330
Which equation defines f?

148
00:09:13,795 --> 00:09:15,285
Pause and try it.

149
00:09:20,056 --> 00:09:22,596
Each output is three times the one before,

150
00:09:22,616 --> 00:09:25,826
so it's exponential with base three.

151
00:09:25,976 --> 00:09:30,586
At x equals zero, f is six,
so six is the starting value.

152
00:09:30,856 --> 00:09:34,275
f of x equals six times three to the x.

153
00:09:34,295 --> 00:09:35,826
The answer is D.

154
00:09:36,338 --> 00:09:40,588
A fits the first two values
only, so always check a third.

155
00:09:40,738 --> 00:09:44,118
Desmos shortcut: enter the
table, then type y one,

156
00:09:44,138 --> 00:09:48,268
tilde, a times b to the x one.

157
00:09:48,497 --> 00:09:52,748
Desmos finds a equals
six and b equals three.

158
00:09:53,177 --> 00:09:57,306
Domain three: problem-solving
and data analysis.

159
00:09:57,577 --> 00:10:00,437
About fifteen percent of the section,

160
00:10:00,457 --> 00:10:03,037
spread across seven skills.

161
00:10:03,057 --> 00:10:05,906
So each skill is a small slice.

162
00:10:06,427 --> 00:10:10,647
Skill nine: ratios, rates,
proportional relationships,

163
00:10:10,667 --> 00:10:11,917
and units.

164
00:10:12,147 --> 00:10:15,966
Expect unit conversions,
rates, and scale problems.

165
00:10:15,986 --> 00:10:18,007
Write the units next to every number,

166
00:10:18,027 --> 00:10:19,397
and let them cancel.

167
00:10:19,868 --> 00:10:24,998
A car is traveling at a constant
speed of sixty-six feet per second.

168
00:10:25,228 --> 00:10:28,237
What is the car's speed in miles per hour?

169
00:10:28,388 --> 00:10:31,998
One mile is five thousand
two hundred eighty feet.

170
00:10:32,467 --> 00:10:33,957
Pause and try it.

171
00:10:39,727 --> 00:10:43,227
Multiply by three thousand
six hundred seconds per hour,

172
00:10:43,247 --> 00:10:44,977
and the seconds cancel.

173
00:10:45,007 --> 00:10:48,987
Then divide by five thousand two
hundred eighty feet per mile,

174
00:10:49,007 --> 00:10:50,346
and the feet cancel.

175
00:10:50,366 --> 00:10:53,056
You get forty-five miles per hour.

176
00:10:53,482 --> 00:10:55,821
Skill ten: percentages.

177
00:10:55,841 --> 00:11:00,332
Percent of a number, percent
change, and percent of a percent.

178
00:11:00,562 --> 00:11:03,621
The key idea: a percent is a multiplier.

179
00:11:03,641 --> 00:11:07,211
One hundred fifty percent
means times one point five.

180
00:11:07,710 --> 00:11:11,480
The number a is one
hundred fifty percent of b,

181
00:11:11,509 --> 00:11:14,440
and b is forty percent of c.

182
00:11:14,830 --> 00:11:17,880
The number a is what percent of c?

183
00:11:18,333 --> 00:11:19,823
Pause and try it.

184
00:11:24,594 --> 00:11:25,974
Multiply the multipliers.

185
00:11:25,994 --> 00:11:29,094
One point five times
point four is point six,

186
00:11:29,114 --> 00:11:31,764
so a is sixty percent of c.

187
00:11:32,074 --> 00:11:34,294
Or pick c equals one hundred.

188
00:11:34,314 --> 00:11:39,213
Then b is forty, and a is one
hundred fifty percent of forty,

189
00:11:39,233 --> 00:11:40,483
which is sixty.

190
00:11:40,886 --> 00:11:46,066
Skill eleven: one-variable data,
distributions and measures of center and

191
00:11:46,086 --> 00:11:46,866
spread.

192
00:11:46,886 --> 00:11:50,226
Mean, median, range, standard deviation,

193
00:11:50,246 --> 00:11:52,666
and plots of one data set.

194
00:11:52,686 --> 00:11:56,896
A favorite question: what happens
when you remove an outlier?

195
00:11:57,350 --> 00:12:01,089
Eight students recorded the minutes
they spent on an assignment:

196
00:12:01,109 --> 00:12:04,770
ten, twelve, fourteen, fourteen, fourteen,

197
00:12:04,790 --> 00:12:07,640
sixteen, eighteen, and ninety.

198
00:12:07,870 --> 00:12:11,880
If the value ninety is removed,
which statement is true?

199
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:13,790
Pause and try it.

200
00:12:19,561 --> 00:12:22,501
Before, the mean is
twenty-three point five,

201
00:12:22,521 --> 00:12:24,491
and the median is fourteen.

202
00:12:24,921 --> 00:12:28,020
Without ninety, the
mean drops to fourteen,

203
00:12:28,040 --> 00:12:30,130
and the median is still fourteen.

204
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:33,821
The mean decreases, and
the median stays the same.

205
00:12:33,841 --> 00:12:35,531
The answer is B.

206
00:12:35,969 --> 00:12:40,029
An outlier pulls the mean a lot
and barely moves the median.

207
00:12:40,049 --> 00:12:44,348
In Desmos, type L equals
the list in square brackets,

208
00:12:44,368 --> 00:12:47,659
then mean of L and median of L.

209
00:12:48,092 --> 00:12:53,192
Skill twelve: two-variable
data, models and scatterplots.

210
00:12:53,212 --> 00:12:56,151
You'll read a line of best
fit, make predictions,

211
00:12:56,171 --> 00:12:59,832
and interpret the slope
and intercept in context.

212
00:12:59,852 --> 00:13:03,262
The line gives predicted
values, not exact ones.

213
00:13:03,743 --> 00:13:06,442
A scatterplot shows the height of a plant,

214
00:13:06,462 --> 00:13:10,363
in centimeters, x weeks
after it was first measured.

215
00:13:10,383 --> 00:13:15,953
The line of best fit is y equals
two point four x plus eighteen.

216
00:13:15,982 --> 00:13:20,713
Which is the best interpretation
of two point four in this context?

217
00:13:21,165 --> 00:13:22,655
Pause and try it.

218
00:13:28,426 --> 00:13:30,246
Two point four is the slope.

219
00:13:30,266 --> 00:13:33,566
It's the change in predicted
height for each extra week.

220
00:13:33,586 --> 00:13:37,805
So the predicted height increases by
two point four centimeters each week.

221
00:13:37,825 --> 00:13:39,716
The answer is C.

222
00:13:40,150 --> 00:13:45,170
Choice A describes the intercept, but
the predicted height at week zero is

223
00:13:45,190 --> 00:13:47,610
eighteen, not two point four.

224
00:13:47,630 --> 00:13:51,760
And at ten weeks, the model
predicts forty-two centimeters.

225
00:13:52,300 --> 00:13:56,510
Skill thirteen: probability
and conditional probability.

226
00:13:56,540 --> 00:13:59,120
Most of these use a two-way table.

227
00:13:59,140 --> 00:14:05,230
Watch for phrases like given that, or if
a student who plays a sport is chosen.

228
00:14:05,420 --> 00:14:08,590
The condition tells you
which total to divide by.

229
00:14:09,085 --> 00:14:14,105
The table shows two hundred students
by grade and whether they play a sport.

230
00:14:14,125 --> 00:14:18,585
In grade ten, forty-eight
play and fifty-two don't.

231
00:14:18,605 --> 00:14:22,855
In grade eleven, thirty-six
play and sixty-four don't.

232
00:14:24,084 --> 00:14:27,775
If a student who plays a
sport is selected at random,

233
00:14:27,885 --> 00:14:31,575
what is the probability that
the student is in grade eleven?

234
00:14:32,011 --> 00:14:33,501
Pause and try it.

235
00:14:40,272 --> 00:14:45,372
The condition is plays a sport, so
the total is everyone who plays:

236
00:14:45,392 --> 00:14:48,082
forty-eight plus
thirty-six, or eighty-four.

237
00:14:48,271 --> 00:14:50,802
Thirty-six of them are in grade eleven.

238
00:14:50,872 --> 00:14:54,292
Thirty-six over eighty-four
is three sevenths.

239
00:14:54,312 --> 00:14:56,042
The answer is D.

240
00:14:56,503 --> 00:15:00,443
Nine fiftieths divides by
all two hundred students.

241
00:15:00,463 --> 00:15:03,793
Nine twenty-fifths
divides by grade eleven.

242
00:15:03,863 --> 00:15:06,633
The condition decides the denominator.

243
00:15:07,057 --> 00:15:12,147
Skill fourteen: inference from sample
statistics and margin of error.

244
00:15:12,377 --> 00:15:16,436
A random sample estimates
something about a whole population.

245
00:15:16,456 --> 00:15:21,466
The margin of error turns that estimate
into a range of plausible values.

246
00:15:21,616 --> 00:15:24,987
Larger samples tend to have
smaller margins of error.

247
00:15:25,409 --> 00:15:30,669
A random sample of four hundred voters
in a city found that fifty-four percent

248
00:15:30,689 --> 00:15:33,019
support building a new park.

249
00:15:33,209 --> 00:15:37,099
The margin of error for this
estimate is three percentage points.

250
00:15:37,449 --> 00:15:41,499
Which conclusion is best
supported by these results?

251
00:15:41,991 --> 00:15:43,481
Pause and try it.

252
00:15:49,252 --> 00:15:53,872
Fifty-four, plus or minus three, gives
fifty-one to fifty-seven percent.

253
00:15:53,892 --> 00:15:57,152
That's a plausible range
for all voters in the city,

254
00:15:57,172 --> 00:15:58,501
not a guarantee.

255
00:15:58,571 --> 00:16:00,262
The answer is A.

256
00:16:00,909 --> 00:16:04,608
B and C both claim exactly
fifty-four percent,

257
00:16:04,628 --> 00:16:06,929
but a sample only gives an estimate.

258
00:16:06,949 --> 00:16:09,679
And D falls outside the range.

259
00:16:10,149 --> 00:16:14,048
Skill fifteen: evaluating
statistical claims,

260
00:16:14,068 --> 00:16:16,999
from observational
studies and experiments.

261
00:16:17,109 --> 00:16:18,398
Two rules.

262
00:16:18,628 --> 00:16:23,249
Random assignment to groups lets
you conclude cause and effect.

263
00:16:23,269 --> 00:16:27,959
Random selection from a population
lets you generalize to that population.

264
00:16:28,499 --> 00:16:33,679
A researcher recruited two hundred
volunteers from one university and randomly

265
00:16:33,699 --> 00:16:39,029
assigned each to either use a
flashcard app daily or not use it.

266
00:16:39,379 --> 00:16:43,999
After four weeks, the app group scored
significantly higher on a vocabulary

267
00:16:44,019 --> 00:16:45,019
test.

268
00:16:45,139 --> 00:16:47,789
Which conclusion is most appropriate?

269
00:16:48,270 --> 00:16:49,760
Pause and try it.

270
00:16:56,531 --> 00:17:00,911
Randomly assigned, so a cause
and effect conclusion is fine.

271
00:17:00,931 --> 00:17:04,630
But the volunteers weren't randomly
selected from all students.

272
00:17:04,650 --> 00:17:09,231
So the conclusion only reaches
students similar to the volunteers.

273
00:17:09,251 --> 00:17:10,860
The answer is C.

274
00:17:11,406 --> 00:17:14,545
B stretches it to every
student in the country.

275
00:17:14,565 --> 00:17:19,336
A says the study can't show cause,
but random assignment allows it.

276
00:17:19,365 --> 00:17:22,696
And D claims something
the study never tested.

277
00:17:23,226 --> 00:17:26,596
Domain four: geometry and trigonometry.

278
00:17:26,985 --> 00:17:29,926
About fifteen percent of the section,

279
00:17:29,946 --> 00:17:34,555
four skills, and this is where
the reference sheet helps most.

280
00:17:34,986 --> 00:17:38,086
Skill sixteen: area and volume.

281
00:17:38,106 --> 00:17:40,566
Composite shapes, missing dimensions,

282
00:17:40,586 --> 00:17:41,796
and scaling.

283
00:17:41,986 --> 00:17:47,205
If every length is multiplied by
k, area is multiplied by k squared,

284
00:17:47,225 --> 00:17:49,395
and volume by k cubed.

285
00:17:49,910 --> 00:17:55,200
A cylinder has a radius of three centimeters
and a height of eight centimeters.

286
00:17:55,230 --> 00:17:59,730
A cone has the same radius and
the same volume as the cylinder.

287
00:17:59,750 --> 00:18:02,799
What is the height of
the cone, in centimeters?

288
00:18:03,249 --> 00:18:04,739
Pause and try it.

289
00:18:10,510 --> 00:18:12,809
Both formulas are on the reference sheet.

290
00:18:12,829 --> 00:18:18,370
The cylinder is pi r squared
h: pi times nine times eight,

291
00:18:18,390 --> 00:18:20,200
or seventy-two pi.

292
00:18:20,350 --> 00:18:23,410
The cone is one third pi r squared h,

293
00:18:23,430 --> 00:18:25,170
which is three pi h.

294
00:18:25,190 --> 00:18:29,240
Three pi h equals seventy-two
pi, so h is twenty-four.

295
00:18:30,118 --> 00:18:35,008
Skill seventeen: lines,
angles, and triangles.

296
00:18:35,158 --> 00:18:39,058
Parallel lines cut by a
transversal, angle sums,

297
00:18:39,078 --> 00:18:42,607
isosceles triangles,
and similar triangles.

298
00:18:42,638 --> 00:18:46,888
Similar triangles have equal
angles and proportional sides.

299
00:18:47,323 --> 00:18:51,813
In triangle A B C, point D is on side A B,

300
00:18:51,843 --> 00:18:58,052
and point E is on side A C, so
that D E is parallel to B C.

301
00:18:58,763 --> 00:19:04,623
If A D is four, D B is
six, and D E is five,

302
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:06,893
what is the length of B C?

303
00:19:07,358 --> 00:19:08,848
Pause and try it.

304
00:19:15,618 --> 00:19:22,078
Because D E is parallel to B C, the small
triangle A D E is similar to the big

305
00:19:22,098 --> 00:19:24,347
triangle A B C.

306
00:19:24,498 --> 00:19:28,157
The big triangle's side
A B is four plus six,

307
00:19:28,177 --> 00:19:29,438
which is ten.

308
00:19:29,458 --> 00:19:33,358
So four over ten equals five over B C,

309
00:19:33,378 --> 00:19:35,988
and B C is twelve point five.

310
00:19:36,518 --> 00:19:40,498
The trap is using D B, six,
instead of the whole side,

311
00:19:40,518 --> 00:19:41,178
A B.

312
00:19:41,198 --> 00:19:42,898
That gives seven point five.

313
00:19:42,918 --> 00:19:46,208
Compare the small triangle
to the whole big triangle.

314
00:19:46,636 --> 00:19:50,375
Skill eighteen: right
triangles and trigonometry.

315
00:19:50,395 --> 00:19:53,136
The Pythagorean theorem,
special right triangles,

316
00:19:53,156 --> 00:19:57,406
soh-cah-toa, complementary
angles, and sometimes radians.

317
00:19:57,918 --> 00:20:02,528
In a right triangle, one of the
acute angles measures thirty degrees.

318
00:20:02,718 --> 00:20:06,888
The side opposite the sixty-degree
angle has a length of nine.

319
00:20:07,118 --> 00:20:09,288
What is the length of the hypotenuse?

320
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:11,270
Pause and try it.

321
00:20:17,041 --> 00:20:20,141
The reference sheet gives the sides: x,

322
00:20:20,161 --> 00:20:23,011
x root three, and two x.

323
00:20:23,281 --> 00:20:26,461
The side opposite sixty is x root three,

324
00:20:26,481 --> 00:20:30,941
so x root three is nine,
and x is three root three.

325
00:20:30,961 --> 00:20:34,541
The hypotenuse is two
x, or six root three.

326
00:20:34,561 --> 00:20:36,411
The answer is B.

327
00:20:36,859 --> 00:20:40,388
Eighteen treats nine as the short side.

328
00:20:40,459 --> 00:20:46,759
Desmos check: in degree mode, nine divided
by sine of sixty is about ten point

329
00:20:46,779 --> 00:20:50,029
three nine, and so is six root three.

330
00:20:50,458 --> 00:20:54,948
Skill nineteen: circles.

331
00:20:55,378 --> 00:21:01,158
Circle equations, arcs and sectors,
central and inscribed angles,

332
00:21:01,178 --> 00:21:03,428
radians, and tangent lines.

333
00:21:03,857 --> 00:21:10,198
The tangent fact to know: a tangent line
is perpendicular to the radius at the

334
00:21:10,218 --> 00:21:11,868
point where it touches.

335
00:21:12,315 --> 00:21:14,735
Point O is the center of a circle.

336
00:21:14,755 --> 00:21:19,135
Line L is tangent to
the circle at point P,

337
00:21:19,155 --> 00:21:21,964
and point Q lies on line L.

338
00:21:22,595 --> 00:21:28,725
If O P is eight and P Q is
fifteen, what is the length of O Q?

339
00:21:29,203 --> 00:21:30,693
Pause and try it.

340
00:21:36,463 --> 00:21:39,762
The radius meets the tangent
line at a right angle,

341
00:21:39,782 --> 00:21:43,483
so triangle O P Q has
its right angle at P.

342
00:21:43,503 --> 00:21:47,643
Eight squared plus fifteen squared
is two hundred eighty-nine,

343
00:21:47,663 --> 00:21:49,993
and the square root is seventeen.

344
00:21:50,450 --> 00:21:53,709
Whenever a circle question
gives you a tangent line,

345
00:21:53,729 --> 00:21:56,860
draw the radius to the point of tangency.

346
00:21:56,970 --> 00:21:59,420
You'll usually get a right triangle.

347
00:21:59,839 --> 00:22:00,899
That's all nineteen.

348
00:22:00,919 --> 00:22:02,928
Here's how to turn it into a plan.

349
00:22:03,118 --> 00:22:06,019
Match every question
you missed to its skill.

350
00:22:06,039 --> 00:22:10,099
Then go to the College Board's free
Question Bank and filter by that exact

351
00:22:10,119 --> 00:22:11,119
skill.

352
00:22:11,368 --> 00:22:13,508
Start with algebra and advanced math,

353
00:22:13,528 --> 00:22:16,188
since they're about seventy
percent of the questions.

354
00:22:16,208 --> 00:22:20,388
And use Desmos where it's
fastest: equations and systems,

355
00:22:20,408 --> 00:22:23,308
sliders, regressions,
equivalent expressions,

356
00:22:23,328 --> 00:22:24,617
and lists.

357
00:22:25,168 --> 00:22:29,308
Here are all nineteen on
one screen, by domain.

358
00:22:29,328 --> 00:22:31,578
Pause here if you want a screenshot.

359
00:22:32,018 --> 00:22:36,558
Every question in this video
was written for this video,

360
00:22:36,578 --> 00:22:39,118
in the style of the real test.

361
00:22:39,138 --> 00:22:41,388
If this helped, subscribe.

362
00:22:41,417 --> 00:22:44,918
The next video goes through
every SAT trap answer,

363
00:22:44,938 --> 00:22:46,868
and how to spot each one.

364
00:22:46,978 --> 00:22:47,978
Good luck.
